      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can confirm that this happening if you follow these directions:\n\n1. Have AMD GPU (Radeon 6800m)\n\n2. Open VRChat\n\n3. Go visit this world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_bd1949f5-54df-4cea-8a58-083eb60bfe33/info\n\n4. Look around, world operates fine\n\n5. Turn on \"Volumetric Lighting\" setting\n\n6. World stutters very badly with bad SteamVR headset timing\n\nCan turn setting on and off to make stuttering go away and come back reliably. This is extremely frustrating because there is no way to know which world will cause this to happen based on lighting.\n\n@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} can someone investigate this? This is a pretty clear cut example of how this bug crops up.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
